  "response": "## The finding: `crime_00060` (`duplicate_component_shape`, hash `e96b55b64336`)\n\nI opened all four locations. The repeated `<div>` is the **form action footer**: a Cancel link plus a submit button. It's identical in every file except the button label:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link\n    href=\"/dashboard/invoices\"\n    className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n  >\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>   {/* or \"Edit Invoice\" */}\n</div>\n```\n\n| File | Lines | Submit label |\n|---|---|---|\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 | Create Invoice |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 | Edit Invoice |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 | Create Invoice |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 | Edit Invoice |\n\nThe forms have already started to drift just above this footer. In final-example, the error `<p>` uses `mt-2` in `create-form.tsx` but `my-2` in `edit-form.tsx`. So the \"edits don't land everywhere\" problem is real, not hypothetical.\n\n## Proposed shared component: `FormActions`\n\n**New file:** `app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n\n```tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\n\nexport type FormActionsProps = {\n  /** Slot: content of the submit button, e.g. \"Create Invoice\". */\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n  /** Where Cancel navigates. Defaults to the invoices list. */\n  cancelHref?: string;\n  /** Slot: Cancel link text. Defaults to \"Cancel\". */\n  cancelLabel?: React.ReactNode;\n  /** Passed through to the submit Button (e.g. disabled / aria-disabled while pending). */\n  submitProps?: Omit<React.ComponentProps<typeof Button>, 'type' | 'children'>;\n};\n\nexport function FormActions({\n  children,\n  cancelHref = '/dashboard/invoices',\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  submitProps,\n}: FormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\" {...submitProps}>\n        {children}\n      </Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Public API:**\n- **`children`** (required slot): the submit label. This is the only thing that actually differs today.\n- **`cancelHref?`**: defaults to `/dashboard/invoices`, the value all four files use now.\n- **`cancelLabel?`** (slot): defaults to `\"Cancel\"`.\n- **`submitProps?`**: passes props through to the existing `Button` (`app/ui/button.tsx`) so a form can add pending or disabled state later without forking the footer. `type` is fixed to `\"submit\"`.\n\n**Call sites after the change:**\n```tsx\n<FormActions>Create Invoice</FormActions>   // create-form.tsx\n<FormActions>Edit Invoice</FormActions>     // edit-form.tsx\n```\nEach form also drops its own `Link` and `Button` imports, if nothing else in the file uses them.\n\n## Files that would change\n\n`final-example` and `starter-example` are separate Next.js apps with no shared package, so `@/` resolves inside each app. That means one copy of the component per app:\n\n1. **New:** `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n2. **New:** `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n3. **Edit:** `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n4. **Edit:** `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n5. **Edit:** `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n6. **Edit:** `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n\nThis removes the duplication *within* each app: the create and edit forms can no longer drift apart. Across the two apps, you'd still have two copies of the component. To get down to one, you'd need a workspace package (e.g. `dashboard/shared-ui`). That's probably not worth it, because `starter-example` is the tutorial's starting point and is meant to differ from `final-example`. The same reasoning applies to the many `exact_duplicate_block` findings that pair starter with final.\n\n**Related, but outside this finding's scope:** the error block above the footer (`<div aria-live=\"polite\">…{state.message}</div>`) is another candidate for a shared component, e.g. `<FormMessage message={state.message} />`. Extracting it would also settle the `mt-2`/`my-2` drift. Separately, `crime_00002` and `crime_00003` (`\"paid\"`/`\"pending\"` checks in the same forms and `status.tsx`) could be fixed alongside by adding an `INVOICE_STATUSES` constant.\n\nI haven't changed any files.",
